  "question": {
    "text": "The number of words that can be written using all the letters of the word \"IRRATIONAL' is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{10 !}{(2 !)^{3}}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{10 !}{(21)^{2}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{10 !}{2 !}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "10 !",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "These are 10 letters in the word IRRATIONAL in which these are $2^{4} I, 2 \\cdot R^{\\prime}$ and $2 \\cdot A^{\\prime}$\r\n$\\therefore$ The total number of word $s=\\frac{10 !}{2 ! 2 ! 2 !}=\\frac{10 !}{(21)^{3}}$"
  }
